WEBVTT

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:03.380
That was so much fun.

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:07.710
This one, too.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:08.510
Okay.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:15.640
Captain.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.180
Shiro.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.390
Is something wrong?

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.400
I was just thinking how much fun
we had at the Equator Festival.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.400
That's not all, is it?

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:34.030
After the ship's repairs are finished, we're
going to participate in Operation: Perseus.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.990
We're just going to back them up, right?

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:41.040
But, there's a chance again of...

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.840
I... The thing is...

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:52.510
I feel like I've finally become a family
with everyone on the Harekaze.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.050
And yet...

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:33.020
May 4th 6:30

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.160
May 5th 1:00

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:45.580
Hello. This is operation headquarters.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:49.330
<i>This is Fukuchi. Has the situation changed?</i>

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.580
Route all the lines over here.

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:53.340
Our over-the-horizon radar at Mt. Fuji's summit
has picked up the Musashi.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.710
<i>But it was headed for the Philippines!</i>

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:01.970
The main force won't reach it in time.
Can your fleet stop the Musashi?

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:01.970
Y118_Musashi

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:03.970
<i>We'll do our best.</i>

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:04.970
<i>I'll call later.</i>

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:12.020
Y118_Musashi

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:14.980
Y467_Harekaze

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:25.990
May 5th 6:10

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:30.000
Harekaze

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:30.000
Musashi

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:36.000
Currently, the Musashi is estimated
to be ten miles south of the Izu Peninsula,

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.260
compass bearing 40 degrees,
at a speed of 18 knots.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.470
We're in pursuit at a speed of 35 knots.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:46.510
Until the Blue Mermaid force arrives,
the school has instructed us

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:48.270
Hello? This is Mashimo Munetani.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:50.770
to continue tracking the Musashi,
while putting our own safety first.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:56.020
Even though we left early this time
so we wouldn't be late.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:00.240
Thanks to that, we're going to be
the closest ship to the Musashi.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:01.860
Ms. Minami.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.200
We should assume
the Musashi students are infected

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.540
with the virus,
just like the Hiei and Spee have been.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.160
Then they can be saved like last time, right?

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:15.210
- I wonder if there's anything we can do?
- I agree.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:18.300
After all, our main battery
has booming new five-inch cannons!

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.880
The command post is brand spanking new, too!

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:29.520
Yeah! And we've got
new model torpedo directors!

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.230
The feel of it! Marvelous!

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:40.900
Thanks to this, we won't have to do
trigonometric functions anymore!

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.740
- I can't wait to fire it!
- G-Good.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:46.120
The water guns were fixed, right?

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:47.160
Of course!

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:50.410
I'm looking for someone to be
my sparring partner with the long sword.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:48.910
Captain?

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:51.500
What shall we do?

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:52.250
We may be able to get up to 50 knots.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.500
Let's follow the school's instructions
and support the Blumers.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:01.300
When it comes to armor and firepower,
the Musashi outclasses us by far.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:05.470
Right. It's best to let
the Blue Mermaids lead the way.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:06.510
I see.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.390
Yeah, of course.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.350
If our opponent is the Musashi...

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:11.140
But let's do our best, everyone!

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:12.390
Let's do our best!

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:13.770
Let's do it!

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:21.400
<i>Our force is south of Ishigaki,
traveling at 40 knots.</i>

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:22.530
May 5th 9:00

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.150
<i>Anyway, we'll move at high speed.</i>

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:27.280
Most of the main force
is east of the Philippines.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:30.370
Gathering our fighting power
backfired on us.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:35.580
<i>The one that'll make it there in time is the
reserve force left off the coast of Kyushu,</i>

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.790
<i>Chief Hiraga's detached force.</i>

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:41.170
Any other ships we can get out there?

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:46.050
<i>There is one ship undergoing maintenance
at the dock, but I don't know if it's ready.</i>

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:52.100
In about three hours, the Musashi
will enter the Uraga Channel.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.640
Absolute Stopping Line

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:55.440
Musashi Main Battery Range

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.060
Where's the Harekaze?

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:01.400
They'll catch up to the Musashi
in approximately two hours.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.400
Y118_Musashi               Y467_Harekaze

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:05.900
<i>I got a ship!</i>

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.410
<i>Ten degrees off the port side,
on the horizon, condition unknown!</i>

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.660
I've got it on radar too!

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:12.410
<i>Bearing angle 90 degrees starboard.</i>

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.910
<i>Flash of light confirmed! The target fired!</i>

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:18.120
Evade it! Hard right rudder!

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.630
Yes, ma'am!

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:24.880
Put some distance between us!

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:26.260
Yes, ma'am!

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.430
Six shells from their main battery, incoming!

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.600
Captain! Should we fire?

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:39.100
It may be easier to evade them
and go serpentine if we fire a warning shot!

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.020
Aye!

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.740
Captain! Your orders...

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:50.370
It's the Blumers!

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:54.120
<i>A message from the Blue Mermaids,</i>

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.750
telling the Harekaze to retreat
from this area immediately!

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.250
Retreat?

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:04.420
<i>An order from the Blue Mermaids to retreat!</i>

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:12.510
Our fleet is going to carry out an operation
to halt the Musashi from off the starboard bow.

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:18.140
Raiding party, remember the crew of the Musashi
are students, so avoid unnecessary fighting.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:23.650
- Commence the operation.
- Commencing the operation!

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:34.620
Fleet, 90 degrees port. Turn around together.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:35.620
Hard left rudder.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:42.540
Their fleet moves together so beautifully.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:46.550
Ship Two, Ship Four,
commence torpedo launch attack.

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:52.300
Commence torpedo launch!

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:11.200
Wow! They're all hitting the mark!

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.450
That may be enough to stop the Musashi...

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:14.120
Captain, a moment.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.620
Take over for a few minutes!

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:21.410
How does the Musashi look?

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:26.040
They've stopped firing, but the damage
is unknown and their speed is the same.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:32.630
Ship One, Ship Three, turn to starboard
together, 90 degrees, and charge!

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:37.560
Ships One and Three,
commence main battery attack.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:38.970
Commence firing!

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.070
The starboard secondary battery target
has been destroyed!

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.610
- All right!
- Aye!

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:57.280
Ship Two, Ship Four,
commence torpedo launch attack.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.410
Commence torpedo launch!

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:05.750
What?

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:06.750
They're malfunctioning?

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:09.590
W-We've got a guidance system error!

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:14.300
What's wrong, Captain?

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:19.140
The Blue Mermaids are here,
but we've got our own role to carry out.

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.060
I don't know...

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.230
<i>...what to do.</i>

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:27.900
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:29.570
Take over here!

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:32.900
Reo, go with the Chief Engineer!

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:33.950
Roger!

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:37.160
- The four of us will keep things together!
- Yes, ma'am!

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:40.870
I heard that electrical systems
will malfunction, but...

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:44.330
Prepare to fire from torpedo tubes.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:45.670
Set it to manual guidance.

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:46.880
Manual guidance?

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.500
First, Second, Third...

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:54.670
We have between 90 and 100 shells
left in the gun turrets.

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:58.550
We're maintaining course,
still heading towards the Uraga Channel.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:12.530
Our ship...

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:15.030
...is attacking the Blue Mermaids.

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:17.990
Let's try to get a grasp of the situation.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:22.120
We'll find a chance to stop the ship. Right?

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:23.790
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:26.210
April 6th 20:00

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:31.800
Nishinoshima New Islands Coast

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:35.170
From tomorrow, we'll be meeting up
with the other classes, huh?

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:36.050
Yeah.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:40.640
Communication to the bridge.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:44.810
Be aware of a freighter 60 degrees to port.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.020
Roger.

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:50.730
Hello?

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:53.020
Is something wrong?

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:55.240
Captain, there's no response.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:07.750
Firing command post, respond!

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:14.880
Captain!

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:18.090
- I'll take a look!
- I'll go, too!

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:22.510
Ms. Tsunada!

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:24.140
Captain!

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:27.020
Calm down. What happened?

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:29.980
Everyone... Everyone is...

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:30.770
Everyone?

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:38.320
What happened to you?

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:42.070
Run!

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:44.080
This way!

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:46.580
April 8th 17:30

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:51.880
So-so, I guess.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:55.210
Captain, I've secured food and water.

00:11:55.710 --> 00:12:01.010
They took over the firing command post,
the engine room, and the wheelhouse.

00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:05.140
We can't even talk to them.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:09.020
It's like they're being controlled by something.

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:15.400
Will this reach them?

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:16.980
Should be no problem.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:22.110
It's being powered by batteries, so I think
we'll only get a few minutes' use out of it.

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:23.740
Go ahead.

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:28.620
This is the Musashi. This is the Musashi.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:33.920
We're currently ten miles northwest
of Asuncion Island. We have an emergency.

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:37.750
We're currently northwest of Asuncion Island.
Northwest of Asuncion Island...

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:39.340
Send help at once...

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:41.050
Send help at once!

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:45.640
Captain. Please come over here.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:47.100
What is it?

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:48.930
A ship from our school.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:54.770
The Harekaze.

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:55.900
Mike?

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:58.150
Set the torpedoes to manual guidance!

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:01.530
First combat speed! Hard right rudder!

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:03.490
Zero degrees, steady as she goes!

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.740
All ships, commence torpedo attack!

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:21.260
Ship Four, impact!

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:22.050
The Blumers!

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:23.760
The Blumers are...

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:26.550
<i>Blumer Ship Four is losing speed!</i>

00:13:27.220 --> 00:13:29.560
Hit! One, two, three, four...

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:31.430
Ship Four's stern took a direct hit!

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:34.020
Report from Ship Four!

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:36.690
"We've been crippled,
unable to continue combat."

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:39.440
We're out of standard torpedoes!

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:43.900
Fleet, go around the target's stern from
starboard. Raid personnel are going to board.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:47.160
All ships, as soon as your drone
is ready, have it take off.

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:55.670
Drones for Ships One, Two
and Three have taken off.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.460
How does the Musashi look?

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.380
The cannons are turning toward the drones.

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:01.380
It seems they're being cautious.

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:05.380
Everyone turn 180 degrees to starboard
while bringing the drones closer.

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.010
Steady as she goes!

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:13.730
Captain! The drones are...

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:20.070
- They're blindfolding us with their drones?
- Amazing!

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:22.530
All ships, commence fire.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.620
Number four secondary cannon
has taken major damage!

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:34.040
The rapid-fire gun?

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:37.540
Hard right rudder!

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:39.630
Full speed retreat!

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:54.770
At this rate...

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:58.310
Ms. Shiretoko, let's back off a little more.

00:14:58.980 --> 00:15:00.690
R-Right!

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:04.690
The Blumers are down to one ship.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:10.280
I wish the Captain and Deputy-Captain
would just get back here!

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:15.450
We have to stop the Musashi.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:18.960
I want to help the Blue Mermaids.

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:23.040
<i>And I want to help everyone
on board the Musashi.</i>

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:29.380
<i>But if we do that...
what if everyone on the Harekaze...</i>

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:32.760
<i>Then I think... what if something
terrible happens?</i>

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:35.100
I'm scared.

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:37.930
I'm terrified!

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:41.400
<i>The Hiraga fleet is down to one ship!</i>

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:46.150
Order all school ships to retreat.

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:47.360
Understood.

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:52.490
Then patch me through a hotline
for the Disaster Management Committee.

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:55.450
What's the evacuation situation?

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:57.870
The entire Tokyo Bay area
has been warned to evacuate.

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:00.120
Emergency Evacuation Information
Marine Safety Support Department Announcement
Please go to a designated disaster evacuation ship.

00:15:58.370 --> 00:16:00.120
But I don't know if there's enough time.

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:04.000
<i>There's a hotline call from
the Yokosuka Girls' Marine High School.</i>

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.000
What?

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:07.630
<i>This is Principal Mayuki Munetani.</i>

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:09.630
<i>I have an announcement.</i>

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:17.180
<i>Under article 12, I'm declaring Yokosuka Girls'
Marine High School to be in a state of emergency.</i>

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:19.270
What?

00:16:19.270 --> 00:16:23.150
<i>And now I'm going to take the bridge,
so if you'll excuse me.</i>

00:16:25.570 --> 00:16:27.780
Seems like we must entrust it to her...

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:30.150
...to Kurushima's Tomoe Gozen.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:31.780
What do you mean?

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:36.830
Fifteen years ago, an armored fleet had been
on a rampage in territorial waters.

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:40.160
The one who annihilated them
with a single ship was that principal.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:43.460
Left rudder.

00:16:48.590 --> 00:16:52.130
<i>We're getting a message from the Blumers.
I'll put it through!</i>

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:56.260
We'll draw the Musashi's attention.
Meanwhile, Harekaze will retreat.

00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:58.770
<i>I repeat, Harekaze, you are to retreat!</i>

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.770
<i>That's the end of the message.</i>

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:03.520
Prepare the minelayer!

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:07.520
There's nothing we can do?

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:11.780
We're going to let the Musashi
enter the Uraga Channel?

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:15.280
Main battery, ready to fire anytime.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:18.030
Bridge, you want to stay at this speed?

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:20.160
Captain, we made rice balls!

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:22.500
<i>- There's curry, too.
- And sweet red-bean soup!</i>

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:23.920
<i>- Captain.
- Captain!</i>

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:29.210
- Flooding in the bow, B2 block!
- Seal it, now!

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:30.960
Captain...

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:36.970
W-We need your orders for
our next move, but... But...

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:39.890
Stop saying butts!

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:42.230
I wasn't! I meant to say,
"but you need to make a decision."

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:47.020
I can't decide on a course of action!

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:51.940
After all, we've always been saved because
things just happened to turn out our way!

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:54.110
It hasn't been because of me!

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:57.660
All of you are my precious family!

00:17:57.660 --> 00:18:00.580
So when I think that I could lose all of you...

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:01.700
...it terrifies me.

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:10.750
That's enough!

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:12.630
Take the captain to the bridge.

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:14.090
R-Right!

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:17.720
You come with me for a bit.

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:24.890
The bridge can't hear us here.

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:27.020
At a time like this, what are you...

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:28.150
Never mind, just drink!

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:33.400
All right, all right!

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:35.070
What I'm trying to say is...

00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:37.910
Eating tuna sashimi with mayonnaise...

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:39.410
is a great combination!

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:45.040
In other words, the Chief Engineer and I
are like night and day.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:47.750
But because two different things are united,

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:50.710
I think it creates something
unique in a good way.

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:52.210
Exactly!

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:56.800
Also, even with a festival drum,
you can't just beat on the skin, right?

00:18:56.800 --> 00:19:00.220
You have to hit the rim too,
or the sound would be missing something!

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:02.850
We're Awesome

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:02.850
Just like me and Kuro!

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:05.350
Isn't that right, Kuro?

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:12.770
I think she's trying to say that true comrades
make up for each other's deficiencies.

00:19:14.230 --> 00:19:18.410
Ms. Munetani, you're the only one
who can help the captain.

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:20.410
Well? Got it?!

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:25.410
Thank you.

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:33.840
Case closed!

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:37.590
Chief Engineer, you really just wanted
to do that, didn't you?

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:46.600
<i>I've got something!</i>

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:48.980
<i>Three shells from their main battery,
coming our way!</i>

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:50.730
- Evade them!
- Right!

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:53.150
Captain!

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:54.730
Deputy-Captain!

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:01.240
I'll...

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:03.580
...be...

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:06.700
...your mayonnaise!

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:09.830
All right! Well said!

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:11.920
As-is, though.

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:14.130
Mayonnaise?

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:17.260
Um, what are you trying to say,
Deputy-Captain?

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:19.510
I want to support the captain!

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:26.010
I want the captain to make decisions like usual,
to act, to bring us luck...

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:29.020
In exchange, I'll try to do...

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:34.020
No, everyone on the Harekaze
will do the rest somehow!

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:37.940
I'm not the only one thinking that.

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:43.570
<i>That's right! We can do more, too!</i>

00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:44.410
<i>Aye!</i>

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:49.080
I-I'm not going to just run away all the time.

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:51.620
<i>I can do anything that needs to be done!</i>

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:53.170
That's right.

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.290
I can do it!

00:20:56.130 --> 00:20:57.300
Where there's a will, there's a way.

00:20:57.550 --> 00:21:01.170
If the Deputy-Captain is mayonnaise,
I'll be mustard!

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:09.850
There is no storm that comrades of the sea
can't overcome, right?

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:11.940
Shiro... Everyone...

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:13.560
Signal with lights from the Musashi!

00:21:13.900 --> 00:21:15.020
<i>I'll read it!</i>

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:17.520
"Keep your distance...

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:21.530
...from our ship.

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:24.030
Approaching is dangerous.

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:27.910
We still have a large supply
of main battery shells."

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.540
"Mo-e-ka."

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:33.250
Moka is safe!

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:35.250
It's all the more reason to save them.

00:21:37.630 --> 00:21:38.630
Isoroku.

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:40.760
Thank you.

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:45.640
Combat...

00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:48.050
...port cannons and torpedoes together.

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:50.640
The Musashi at 300 degrees!

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:57.150
The target, compass bearing 30 degrees,
speed 18 knots!

00:21:57.560 --> 00:22:00.480
Fifth combat speed, 340 degrees,
steady as she goes!

00:22:02.860 --> 00:22:05.660
Captain. The Harekaze is sending
a flashing light signal!

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:10.660
- Read it.
- Yes.

00:22:11.790 --> 00:22:14.540
"We are coming to rescue your ship.

00:22:14.710 --> 00:22:17.960
I repeat, we're coming to rescue your ship."

00:22:19.040 --> 00:22:25.050
Episode 11:
In a Pinch with a Battleship's Big Cannon!
